{"name":"Virgin Olive Oil","hex":"#e2dcab","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"virgin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who has never had sexual intercourse, or  an animal that has never mated.","A person who has never engaged in any sexual activity at all. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In a state of virginity; chaste, not having had sexual intercourse.","Of a physical object, untouched."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virgin"},{"term":"olive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree of species Olea europaea cultivated since ancient times in the Mediterranean for its fruit and the oil obtained from it.","The small oval fruit of this tree, eaten ripe (usually black) or unripe (usually green)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a grayish green color, that of an unripe olive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/olive"},{"term":"oil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Liquid fat.","Petroleum-based liquid used as fuel or lubricant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lubricate with oil.","To grease with oil for cooking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Olive oil","blocks":[{"text":"Olive oil is a vegetable oil obtained by pressing whole olives and extracting the oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Oliven_V1.jpg/330px-Oliven_V1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive_oil","wikidata":"Q93165"},{"title":"Olive","blocks":[{"text":"The cultivated olive is a subspecies of subtropical evergreen tree in the family Oleaceae. Modern cultivars are traced primarily to the Near East, Aegean Sea, and Strait of Gibraltar. Olea europaea is the type species for its genus, Olea, which lends its name to the Oleaceae plant family. The olive fruit is classed botanically as a drupe, similar in structure and function to the cherry or peach. The term oil was originally synonymous with olive oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Olivesfromjordan.jpg/330px-Olivesfromjordan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive","wikidata":"Q1621080"},{"title":"Oil","blocks":[{"text":"Oil is a liquid with varying degrees of viscosity depending on temperature. Oil is any nonpolar chemical substance that is composed primarily of hydrocarbons and is hydrophobic and lipophilic. Oils are usually flammable and surface active. Most oils are unsaturated lipids that are liquid at room temperature."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil","wikidata":"Q42962"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Oliven_V1.jpg/500px-Oliven_V1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Oliven_V1.jpg/1280px-Oliven_V1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Oliven_V1.jpg/500px-Oliven_V1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOliven_V1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Klazomenai.jpg/500px-Klazomenai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Klazomenai.jpg/500px-Klazomenai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ancient Greek olive oil production workshop in Klazomenai, Ionia (modern Turkey)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKlazomenai.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Turkey.Bodrum042.jpg/500px-Turkey.Bodrum042.jpg?utm_sou